 "fieldData": {
  "awb---faq-data": "<div data-rt-embed-type='true'><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><script> window.awbFAQ = {\"heading\": \"App Landing Page Questions, Answered\", \"items\": [{\"q\": \"What is an app landing page?\", \"a\": \"An app landing page is a single web page that introduces an app and asks for one action: download it, or sign up. Ads, emails, and QR codes all point to it. A good mobile app landing page shows the app on real screens and keeps the download one tap away.\"}, {\"q\": \"How to design a landing page for an app?\", \"a\": \"Good app landing page design starts with one action. Put a plain headline and the store badges at the top, show three or four current screens in phone frames, and give laptop visitors a QR code in place of the badges. With Emergent's <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-landing-page-builder'>AI landing page builder</a>, you describe that layout in a prompt and get the page plus a table that logs each badge tap.\"}, {\"q\": \"What is a good landing page for mobile apps?\", \"a\": \"The strongest ones make the app's purpose plain before the visitor scrolls. Screenshots come from the version people can install today, and the badge for the visitor's phone sits within thumb reach. Reviews stay short, and no pop-up hides the content on a first visit.\"}, {\"q\": \"What do the best app landing pages include?\", \"a\": \"The best app landing pages share four parts: a headline that names one job, real screens in phone frames, a short review or two, and badges at the top and bottom. Example galleries sort them by category, which makes it quick to study apps close to yours.\"}, {\"q\": \"Is an app landing page template enough to launch with?\", \"a\": \"A template covers the layout and little else. It gives you sections and phone frames, but the headline, the screenshots, the badge links, and any device routing are still yours to supply. With Emergent, a prompt that names your app and its stores produces the page with the routing and the click table already in place.\"}, {\"q\": \"What is an application landing page for a web app?\", \"a\": \"An application landing page for a web app asks for a sign-up instead of a store visit. The form should ask only for what the first session needs, often an email address and a password, and then open the product. Most of these pages also link to a <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-landing-page-builder/pricing-page'>pricing page</a> for buyers who compare plans before they commit.\"}, {\"q\": \"How does an app landing page send each phone to the right store?\", \"a\": \"An app download landing page checks the visitor's operating system as the page loads. iPhones get the App Store badge and Android phones get Google Play, each linked to the app's own listing and not to a store search. Anyone on a laptop gets a QR code to scan with their phone.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do you track clicks on a mobile app landing page?\", \"a\": \"Add UTM tags to each link you share, and record every badge tap with the campaign it came from. On a mobile app landing page, that tap is the last step you can measure; installs are counted by the store. Emergent builds the page so each tap lands as a row in a database you own.\"}, {\"q\": \"Can I make a landing page for my app before it launches?\", \"a\": \"Yes. Before launch, the page collects emails for a waitlist where the store badges will go, and each sign-up lands on a thank you page that can ask for a referral. On release day, swap the form for the badges and email the list once.\"}, {\"q\": \"What is the difference between an app landing page and a website?\", \"a\": \"An app landing page asks for one action and drops the navigation, while a website has many pages for many readers: support, careers, pricing, and press. Plenty of apps launch with the landing page alone and add a site once help docs pile up. Some grow into a <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-landing-page-builder/one-page-website'>one page website</a> first, with a section per feature.\"}]}; </script></div></div>"
 }
